aarch64: detect native CPU from /proc/cpuinfo instead of system registers

Reading the ID_AA64* system registers (e.g. midr_el1) from EL0 requires the
kernel to trap or emulate those accesses. Linux only started emulating them
in 4.11, so on older kernels (e.g. the 4.9 kernel of some Android devices)
any zig invocation that performs native CPU detection dies with SIGILL.

Use the already-existing /proc/cpuinfo parser (which supports the aarch64
cpuinfo format and is unit-tested) for aarch64 instead.

diff --git a/zig/lib/std/zig/system/linux.zig b/zig/lib/std/zig/system/linux.zig
--- a/zig/lib/std/zig/system/linux.zig
+++ b/zig/lib/std/zig/system/linux.zig
@@ -458,23 +458,10 @@
             return ArmCpuinfoParser.parse(current_arch, &file_reader.interface) catch null;
         },
         .aarch64, .aarch64_be => {
-            const registers = [12]u64{
-                getAArch64CpuFeature("MIDR_EL1"),
-                getAArch64CpuFeature("ID_AA64PFR0_EL1"),
-                getAArch64CpuFeature("ID_AA64PFR1_EL1"),
-                getAArch64CpuFeature("ID_AA64DFR0_EL1"),
-                getAArch64CpuFeature("ID_AA64DFR1_EL1"),
-                getAArch64CpuFeature("ID_AA64AFR0_EL1"),
-                getAArch64CpuFeature("ID_AA64AFR1_EL1"),
-                getAArch64CpuFeature("ID_AA64ISAR0_EL1"),
-                getAArch64CpuFeature("ID_AA64ISAR1_EL1"),
-                getAArch64CpuFeature("ID_AA64MMFR0_EL1"),
-                getAArch64CpuFeature("ID_AA64MMFR1_EL1"),
-                getAArch64CpuFeature("ID_AA64MMFR2_EL1"),
-            };
-
-            const core = @import("arm.zig").aarch64.detectNativeCpuAndFeatures(current_arch, registers);
-            return core;
+            // Reading these system registers from EL0 requires kernel
+            // emulation that only exists on Linux >= 4.11; older kernels
+            // raise SIGILL here. /proc/cpuinfo works everywhere.
+            return ArmCpuinfoParser.parse(current_arch, &file_reader.interface) catch null;
         },
         .sparc, .sparc64 => {
             return SparcCpuinfoParser.parse(current_arch, &file_reader.interface) catch null;
         },
